      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(ui): add mock chat fixtures for design QA",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Control UI mock has limited curated chat state for design QA, so reviewers have to rely on ad hoc sessions when checking empty chat, longer transcripts, markdown rendering, code blocks, tables, warnings, and recoverable error copy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis PR adds stable dev/mock-only fixture sessions to the Control UI mock server. The proposed fixtures cover a New session empty state, a coding session, a response-shape showcase, and a markdown showcase without changing production gateway or session APIs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no production user-facing behavior change. Developers and designers can load stable mock chat sessions for future Control UI visual review.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 scripts/control-ui-mock-dev.ts`\n- `pnpm run dev:ui:mock -- --port 55237`\n- System Chrome smoke loaded these mock routes and confirmed each requested `chat.startup` with the matching session key:\n  - `/chat?session=agent%3Aopenclaw-mock%3Anew-session`\n  - `/chat?session=agent%3Aopenclaw-mock%3Aqa-coding-session`\n  - `/chat?session=agent%3Aopenclaw-mock%3Aresponse-shape-showcase`\n  - `/chat?session=agent%3Aopenclaw-mock%3Amarkdown-showcase`\n",
        "branch": "brzezowski/control-ui-mock-fixtures",
